review_comments.body:
 I believe this test is wrong even though it passes. The rule it's testing, `TOPIC;.*;;;;;READ;ALLOW;User:alice`, contains 8 semicolons, so it has 9 fields, and `parse` uses `split(SEPARATOR, 6)`, which stops after the first 5 semicolons and puts everything that's left into the last part. If the test checked the full `MirrorAclRule`, it would fail because:
- the operation is `null` (any) instead of `READ`;
- the permission type is `null` (any) instead of `ALLOW`;
- the principal is `;READ;ALLOW;User:alice` instead of `User:alice`.

The input here should be `TOPIC;.*;;READ;ALLOW;User:alice`. Maybe assert the full rule so it catches this kind of drift in the future, WDYT?

